PREAMBLE / 序言
中文
本作品的创作与公开分享，不以获取经济利益为目的。
创造可以源于好奇、兴趣、求知、探索以及创造本身的欲望。知识、思想与技术成果不应当只能通过商业交换才能进入人们的生活。
本许可希望保留并传播一种可能性：
人可以自由创造，自由分享，自由使用他人的创造物，而不必将一切创造活动转化为商业活动。
本许可不要求使用者赞同作者的思想，也不要求使用者接受某种组织、制度或社会主张。
但是，如果你选择接受本作品所提供的自由，就必须同时接受本许可规定的使用条件。
你可以不使用本作品，但不能在接受本作品的同时，单方面取消本许可所规定的条件。
本许可不是为了建立新的商业模式，也不是为了使作者从作品的传播中获得经济利益。它是作者选择如何给予自己的创造物的一份公开声明。
English
The creation and public sharing of this Work are not intended to generate economic profit.
Creation may arise from curiosity, interest, the pursuit of knowledge, exploration, or the desire to create itself. Knowledge, ideas, and technological achievements should not have to pass through commercial exchange in order to become accessible to people.
This License seeks to preserve and communicate a possibility:
People can create freely, share freely, and use the creations of others without turning every creative activity into a commercial activity.
This License does not require Recipients to agree with the Author's beliefs, nor does it require them to accept any particular organization, institution, or social doctrine.
However, anyone who chooses to accept the freedoms offered by this Work must also accept the conditions established by this License.
You are free not to use this Work. You may not accept the permissions granted by this License while unilaterally discarding its conditions.
This License is not intended to establish a new business model or generate economic returns for the Author through the distribution of the Work. It is a public declaration of how the Author chooses to give their creation.

1. DEFINITIONS / 定义
中文
在本许可中：
1.1 原作品（Original Work）
指由许可授予者拥有或有权授权，并明确以本许可发布的软件、源代码及其相关材料。
1.2 使用者（Recipient）
指通过下载、复制、运行、修改、传播或其他方式取得本作品的人或组织。
1.3 修改作品（Modified Work）
指对原作品进行实质性修改、扩展、改编、重构，或将原作品的实质性代码纳入其中而形成的作品。
1.4 源代码（Source Code）
指开发者修改作品时所使用的首选形式，包括理解、修改、构建和运行该作品所合理需要的源文件、构建脚本、配置及相关材料。
1.5 商业目的（Commercial Purpose）
指直接或间接以获取经济收益、商业竞争优势或服务于营利性经营活动为目的的使用行为。
1.6 商业主体（Commercial Entity）
指以营利经营为目的的企业、公司、商业组织，以及代表其利益行事的关联主体或其他组织。
1.7 非营利组织（Non-Profit Organization）
指依法设立且不以向成员、所有者或控制人分配利润为目的的组织。其使用仍须满足第四条的条件。
English
For the purposes of this License:
1.1 Original Work
Means the software, source code, and associated materials owned or lawfully licensed by the Licensor and expressly released under this License.
1.2 Recipient
Means any individual or organization that obtains the Work through downloading, copying, running, modifying, distributing, or other means.
1.3 Modified Work
Means a work resulting from substantial modification, extension, adaptation, or restructuring of the Original Work, or from incorporating substantial portions of its code.
1.4 Source Code
Means the preferred form in which developers modify the Work, including source files, build scripts, configuration files, and associated materials reasonably necessary to understand, modify, build, and run the Work.
1.5 Commercial Purpose
Means any use directly or indirectly intended to obtain economic profit, commercial competitive advantage, or to serve profit-oriented business activities.
1.6 Commercial Entity
Means any company, enterprise, business organization, or other entity operating for profit, as well as any affiliated entity or other organization acting on its behalf or for its benefit.
1.7 Non-Profit Organization
Means an organization legally established without the purpose of distributing profits to its members, owners, or controllers. Its use remains subject to the conditions in Section 4.
1. GRANT OF PERMISSIONS / 授权范围
中文
在遵守本许可全部条款的前提下，许可授予者授予使用者全球范围内、非独占、免许可费、不可转让的有限授权，允许使用者：
下载、安装、复制和运行原作品；
阅读、研究和学习原作品的源代码；
为个人非商业目的修改原作品；
在符合本许可条件的前提下，传播原作品及修改作品；
在符合本许可条件的前提下，基于原作品进行进一步创造。
除本许可明确授予的权利外，其他权利均不在本许可授权范围内。
English
Subject to full compliance with this License, the Licensor grants each Recipient a worldwide, non-exclusive, royalty-free, non-transferable, limited license to:
Download, install, copy, and run the Original Work;
Read, study, and learn from its Source Code;
Modify the Original Work for personal, non-commercial purposes;
Distribute the Original Work and Modified Works subject to this License;
Create further works based on the Original Work subject to this License.
No rights are granted beyond those expressly stated in this License.
1. PERSONAL AND NON-COMMERCIAL USE / 个人及非商业使用
中文
自然人可以将本作品用于个人学习、研究、实验、娱乐及其他非商业目的。
个人使用者不得：
将本作品用于直接或间接获取商业收益的活动；
将本作品用于履行企业或商业组织的工作职责；
代表企业或商业主体使用本作品；
将本作品用于为商业主体提供产品、服务、技术支持或竞争优势；
通过本作品向他人提供收费服务或商业化解决方案。
使用者的个人身份不构成商业使用的豁免。
判断使用性质时，应综合考虑实际目的、受益主体以及使用行为与商业活动之间的关系，而不只考虑使用者的身份或是否直接收费。
English
Individuals may use the Work for personal learning, research, experimentation, entertainment, and other non-commercial purposes.
Individual Recipients shall not:
Use the Work in activities directly or indirectly intended to generate commercial revenue;
Use the Work in performing duties for a company or commercial organization;
Use the Work on behalf of a commercial entity;
Use the Work to provide products, services, technical support, or competitive advantages to a commercial entity;
Provide paid services or commercial solutions to others through the Work.
An individual's personal status does not exempt an otherwise commercial use.
The nature of a use shall be assessed by considering its actual purpose, its beneficiary, and its relationship to commercial activities, rather than merely the user's identity or whether a direct fee is charged.
1. NON-PROFIT ORGANIZATIONS / 非营利组织
中文
非营利组织可以使用本作品，但必须同时满足以下条件：
使用行为不以获取商业利润为目的；
不将本作品用于商业经营或商业产品开发；
不以本作品为基础向公众提供收费软件、收费服务或其他收费成果；
基于本作品产生的修改作品及相关源代码，必须按照本许可公开；
不得将本作品或其修改作品交由商业主体用于商业目的；
不得通过关联组织、合作方或其他第三方规避上述限制。
非营利组织的登记身份本身并不自动构成使用授权。实际使用行为必须满足本条全部条件。
English
Non-profit organizations may use the Work only if all of the following conditions are met:
The use is not intended to generate commercial profit;
The Work is not used for commercial operations or commercial product development;
No paid software, paid services, or other paid deliverables based on the Work are offered to the public;
All Modified Works and associated Source Code derived from the Work are released in accordance with this License;
The Work or any Modified Work is not provided to a Commercial Entity for commercial purposes;
These restrictions are not circumvented through affiliated organizations, partners, or other third parties.
Non-profit registration alone does not automatically grant permission to use the Work. All actual uses must satisfy every condition of this Section.
1. PUBLICATION OF MODIFICATIONS / 修改作品的公开义务
中文
任何获得本作品授权并进行实质性修改的使用者，都必须公开修改后的完整对应源代码。
该义务不以修改作品是否对外分发为前提。
使用者应当：
自实质性修改完成之日起三十日内，公开修改后的完整源代码；
提供足以使他人理解、修改和构建该修改作品的相关文件；
在公开位置附带本许可全文；
保留原作品的版权声明及许可声明；
明确标注修改者、修改日期及主要修改内容；
不得通过加密、混淆、拆分或其他技术手段故意阻止他人获取和研究源代码。
公开方式应当使公众能够免费、合理地获取相关源代码，不得以付费、会员资格或商业授权作为获取条件。
如果使用者因法律义务、保密义务或其他不可避免的限制而无法履行本条公开义务，则其不得进行相应修改或继续使用该修改作品，除非事先获得许可授予者的书面例外授权。
本条不要求公开与原作品无关的个人资料、密码、密钥、私人信息或依法不得公开的第三方材料。使用者不得以此为由将本应公开的修改代码整体封闭；如无法合理分离，则不得进行相关修改或使用。
English
Any Recipient who makes substantial modifications to the Work under this License must publicly release the complete corresponding Source Code of the Modified Work.
This obligation applies regardless of whether the Modified Work is distributed to others.
The Recipient shall:
Publicly release the complete modified Source Code within thirty (30) days after completing substantial modifications;
Provide the materials reasonably necessary for others to understand, modify, and build the Modified Work;
Include the full text of this License in the public release;
Preserve the copyright and license notices of the Original Work;
Clearly identify the modifier, modification date, and principal changes;
Not deliberately prevent access to or study of the Source Code through encryption, obfuscation, fragmentation, or other technical means.
The Source Code shall be made reasonably and freely accessible to the public. No payment, membership, or commercial authorization may be required to obtain it.
If the Recipient is unable to comply with this publication obligation due to legal duties, confidentiality obligations, or other unavoidable restrictions, the Recipient shall not make the relevant modifications or continue using the Modified Work unless a written exception has been granted in advance by the Licensor.
This Section does not require the disclosure of unrelated personal data, passwords, keys, private information, or third-party materials that may not lawfully be disclosed. However, this exception shall not be used to withhold the Modified Work as a whole. If the required materials cannot reasonably be separated, the relevant modification or use shall not be undertaken.
1. STRONG COPYLEFT AND SAME-LICENSE REQUIREMENT / 强传染性与相同许可要求
中文
任何基于本作品形成的修改作品及衍生作品，在公开传播时，必须整体采用本许可。
使用者不得：
删除或弱化本许可中的非商业限制；
允许企业或商业主体使用本作品及其衍生部分；
取消修改作品的源代码公开义务；
将本作品或其衍生部分改为允许商业使用或封闭源代码的许可；
通过更换项目名称、调整文件结构、拆分模块或其他形式上的改变规避本条。
本条适用于与原作品形成实质性衍生关系的部分，不自动扩展到仅仅独立存在、通过普通接口交互或与本作品进行简单聚合的独立作品。
English
Any Modified Work or derivative work based on the Original Work must, when publicly distributed, be licensed as a whole under this License.
Recipients shall not:
Remove or weaken the non-commercial restrictions of this License;
Permit Commercial Entities to use the Work or its derivative portions;
Remove the Source Code publication obligation;
Re-license the Work or its derivative portions under terms that permit commercial use or closed-source distribution;
Circumvent this Section through renaming, restructuring, module separation, or other formal changes.
This Section applies to portions that are substantively derived from the Original Work. It does not automatically extend to independent works that merely exist separately, interact through ordinary interfaces, or are simply aggregated with the Work.
1. FREE REDISTRIBUTION / 免费传播
中文
任何符合本许可条件的使用者，都可以免费复制、传播和分享本作品及其修改作品。
传播时必须：
保留原始版权声明；
附带本许可全文；
明确标注修改情况；
不得施加与本许可相冲突的额外限制；
确保接收者能够免费获取相应源代码。
任何使用者不得将本作品或其修改作品转化为必须通过付费、商业授权或其他排他性条件才能获得的资源。
English
Any Recipient who complies with this License may freely copy, distribute, and share the Original Work and Modified Works without charge.
When redistributing the Work, the Recipient shall:
Preserve the original copyright notices;
Include the full text of this License;
Clearly identify any modifications;
Not impose additional restrictions inconsistent with this License;
Ensure that the corresponding Source Code is freely accessible to Recipients.
No Recipient may transform the Work or any Modified Work into a resource that can only be obtained through payment, commercial authorization, or other exclusive conditions.
